Package: xclim
Type: Package
Title: Bioclimatic Variables from Monthly Climate Data
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Angel Luis", "Robles Fernandez",
                   email = "a.l.robles.fernandez@gmail.com",
                   role = c("aut", "cre"),
                   comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-4835-2741"))
Description: Computes the 19 standard bioclimatic variables (BIO01-BIO19) from
    monthly climate data following the WorldClim specification
    (Hijmans et al. 2005) <doi:10.1002/joc.1276>. Provides both individual
    variable functions and a unified interface to compute all 19 variables at
    once. Includes an ERA5-Land hourly-to-monthly aggregation pipeline for
    converting raw reanalysis data to monthly variables (tas, tasmax, tasmin,
    pr). Supports single-pixel vectors and block-based raster processing via
    'terra' for memory-efficient handling of large spatial datasets. The C++
    backend uses 'xtensor' for high-performance array operations with OpenMP
    parallelism.
